    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW26bA1YeWLoVkyeLuWM5JLJh)_\n\n## Why the search failed\n\n`[]` is the empty vector of enabled sources: `consult-omni--multi-lookup` takes `(aref sources 0)` and there were none. Cause was in the config, not the package: `(require 'consult-omni-sources)` only defines the loader, and the call to `consult-omni-sources-load-modules` sat in a `:tangle no` block, so no source was ever defined and every name in `consult-omni-multi-sources` was silently dropped. (A source is also dropped while its API key, program or package is missing, so a list of only such names fails the same way.)\n\n## What\n\n- Vendored copy of consult-omni in `libraries/modules/cloned/consult-omni/` (GPL-3.0-or-later; upstream ships no LICENSE file, so the GPL text is added and every file keeps its header). `VENDORED.org` has the upstream commit and the two local patches (a clear `user-error` instead of `aref` on an empty vector).\n- `sp-browsing`: loads that copy with `:ensure nil` + `:load-path` (same pattern as `sp-consult-snapfile`; this is a deliberate exception to the Elpaca rule because you asked for the source in the config), calls the loader in `:config`, ends with `provide`, and is added to `sp-late-modules`.\n- The three scope commands passed `args` where `consult-omni-multi` expects `min-input`; they now share one helper.\n- TODOs: API keys in `var/consult-omni-secrets.el` (ignored by Git); a `Vulpea` title source for `consult-omni-local`; `sp-fetch-academic-omni` (`C-c w b s`) sends a scholar result to `sp-fetch-academic-doi` or `-download`. Left as TODO with notes: DEVONthink, sp-trails integration, results in another buffer, launcher.\n- Google Scholar: comparison in the `sp-browsing` doc. Recommendation: keep `biblio-gscholar`; use OpenAlex/PubMed/Scopus through consult-omni, joined at the DOI. Scholar has no API, and a keystroke-driven source would scrape it repeatedly and hit CAPTCHAs.\n\n## Heads up\n\n- The old doc had a real-looking Google Custom Search key in a commented line. Removed, but it is in Git history: rotate it if it is real.\n- Rebasing onto `main` brought in the litdb block from #197; the doc and `.el` agree (tangle check passes).\n\n## Tested\n\nEmacs 29.3 batch: vendored files read without syntax errors, the new guard signals the `user-error` on an empty vector, `tools/check-tangle.sh` passes. Not run: a real consult-omni session (the container cannot reach MELPA/ELPA), the Vulpea source, `sp-fetch-academic-omni`. A first search on the Mac is the real test.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiAn4WtUefbCv1hoZoL)_",
